  "summary": "Ashland (WI) Police Department will not renew its one-year Flock Safety ALPR contract and is having the cameras removed, citing significant downtime and concerns about Flock's responsiveness. Chief Brandon Marten said the decision, made months ago, also acknowledged community concerns about the technology.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Ashland Police Department has decided to not renew its contract for Flock Safety cameras and will be removing the surveillance system.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "they have experienced significant periods of downtime where the cameras were frequently unavailable for use in investigations",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "As the contract reaches its natural conclusion, it provides an opportunity to remove the current system and thoughtfully reevaluate the technologies available to law enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    }
